## 1. The four widths already have distinct implementations

### spaCy / 8D

- [SpaCyModalDecoder.decode_embedding](/home/barberb/lift_coding/external/ipfs_datasets/ipfs_datasets_py/optimizers/logic_theorem_optimizer/spacy_modal_codec.py:2087) hashes the linguistic feature stream into a configurable number of bins, default 8; sums contributions; normalizes; and rounds coordinates to six decimals.
- [_feature_stream](/home/barberb/lift_coding/external/ipfs_datasets/ipfs_datasets_py/optimizers/logic_theorem_optimizer/spacy_modal_codec.py:2182) includes document length, eligible lemmas, POS/dependency tags, modal cues, and modal-family counts. These are hash buckets with collisions, not eight separately named semantic coordinates.
- [LinguisticAutoencoder](/home/barberb/lift_coding/external/ipfs_datasets/ipfs_datasets_py/optimizers/logic_theorem_optimizer/autoencoder_lineages/legacy_v1/linguistic.py:100) preserves separate `historical_blank_en` and `local_en_core_web_sm` backends. The local richer backend refuses fallback. It binds pipeline/package/codec identity into `linguistic:spacy-feature-hash8d:<digest>`.
- The explicit legacy profile refuses attaching a learned formula head through its constructor. Do not erase that boundary to fit the new plan.

The meaning of this source-defined 8D producer is now identified. Which retained/runtime instance the next experiment selects still needs exact identity and admission.

### GTE-small / 384D

- [autoencoder_embedding_production](/home/barberb/lift_coding/external/ipfs_datasets/ipfs_datasets_py/optimizers/logic_theorem_optimizer/autoencoder_embedding_production.py:26) pins `thenlper/gte-small` revision `17e1f347d17fe144873b1201da91788898c639cd`, dimension 384, mean pooling, L2 normalization, CPU float32, and a 512-token ceiling without truncation.
- [autoencoder_embedding_runtime](/home/barberb/lift_coding/external/ipfs_datasets/ipfs_datasets_py/optimizers/logic_theorem_optimizer/autoencoder_embedding_runtime.py:298) owns bounded offline native receipt production.
- [source_embeddings_384.embed_texts](/home/barberb/lift_coding/external/ipfs_datasets/ipfs_datasets_py/logic/formalization/autoencoder/source_embeddings_384.py:53) reuses verified cached assets and explicitly checks full token count; its inference path can use an available CUDA device, separate from the receipt producer's CPU contract.
- [artifacts_and_inputs.md](/home/barberb/lift_coding/external/ipfs_datasets/docs/autoencoders/artifacts_and_inputs.md) already specifies verified manifests, source selectors, split identities, exact float32 values, retained rejection dispositions, and the no-mock/no-download rule.

This is a concrete pinned producer contract, not merely a public-model candidate. Local assets and receipts were not replayed in this research.

