## 2. There are already multiple learned-decoder families

### Reviewed pretrained Torch route

The actual canonical file is [autoencoder_training_worker.py](/home/barberb/lift_coding/external/ipfs_datasets/ipfs_datasets_py/optimizers/logic_theorem_optimizer/autoencoder_training_worker.py:657), not the Intent IR wire parser.

The current observed worker is 312136 bytes, SHA-256 `f1d6369a6f07bb5d42b4695af9c7a1595a2b68eae217529173a7f0787ce13c0a`. This differs from the earlier held 316963-byte metadata; preserve both source epochs rather than silently rebinding old checkpoints.

- `ReviewedDecoderTrainingJobSpec` binds source/stage/exposure/model/tokenizer/license artifacts, base model and optimizer checkpoints, parent checkpoint, input/split hashes, backend identity, and source pins.
- `ReviewedMixedDecoderTrainingJobSpec` adds explicit mixed admission.
- `ReviewedDecoderRuntime` requires caller-owned admission, execution and asset-policy guards plus existing registry and backend methods.
- [TorchReviewedDecoderBackend](/home/barberb/lift_coding/external/ipfs_datasets/ipfs_datasets_py/optimizers/logic_theorem_optimizer/autoencoder_training_worker.py:2706) accepts injected model/optimizer/tokenizer, supports explicit `encoder_decoder` and `causal_lm` architectures, and rejects unsupported device/layout combinations. It does not fetch or admit models.
- It exposes `identity`, `validate_training_records`, `inspect_checkpoint`, `restore_checkpoint`, `restored_checkpoint_matches`, `snapshot_checkpoint`, `train_batch`, and `generate_batch`.
- [train_batch](/home/barberb/lift_coding/external/ipfs_datasets/ipfs_datasets_py/optimizers/logic_theorem_optimizer/autoencoder_training_worker.py:3174) implements supervised updates with finite-loss/gradient checks, clipping, optimizer progress, and tokenization/conditioning identity checks. This is not a generic RL or embedding-distillation interface.

The [current handoff](/home/barberb/lift_coding/external/ipfs_datasets/ipfs_datasets_py/logic/autoformal/docs/HANDOFF.md:6) records explicit Qwen2 prompt/body/EOS matching, recipe/checkpoint separation, fixture state/resume qualification, and an open gate for current-source actual pretrained pair/capacity qualification before separately admitted fitting. Its recorded 93-case result is historical engineering evidence, not a test rerun here or a pretrained-convergence result.

### Retained compact source384 routes

- [source_training_v2](/home/barberb/lift_coding/external/ipfs_datasets/ipfs_datasets_py/logic/formalization/autoencoder/source_training_v2.py:267) exposes `train`, `Runtime`, `evaluate`, and `load_checkpoint` for an experimental source384-to-typed-IR route. Baseline and semantic strategies share inherited weights, vocabulary, transform, and batching; semantic selection uses free-running tuning predictions.
- [structured_source_384](/home/barberb/lift_coding/external/ipfs_datasets/ipfs_datasets_py/logic/formalization/autoencoder/structured_source_384.py:195) is a different fixed-schema decoder: a frozen inherited residual projection feeds learned scalar classifiers. Variable schemas, array lengths, and unseen classes are explicit frontiers.
- These are existing baselines with distinct representational capacity. Do not label them interchangeable with complete variable-structure autoregressive decoding.

The [checkpoint representation study](/home/barberb/lift_coding/external/ipfs_datasets/docs/autoencoders/alignment_checkpoint_representations.md) documents a selected trained 384D residual projector and formula conditioning state, with three projection-only endpoints. Its 8D residual branch requires a 384D skip input; it is not the separate spaCy8 representation or a complete 8D compressed code. The selected 32D condition is not a proof embedding. Its full donor loader has a source-pin compatibility refusal that a separate projection-only reader does not override.

