## Follow-up: existing distillation and weight-transfer experiments

Further read-only inspection located these exact integration points:

- [decoder_distillation_experiment.run_trial](/home/barberb/lift_coding/external/ipfs_datasets/ipfs_datasets_py/logic/formalization/autoencoder/decoder_distillation_experiment.py:414) already supports private development-only same-codec continuation/distillation. `_loss` at line206 computes masked reference-prefix CE plus alpha-weighted KL from detached teacher logits. Teacher/student logits must have identical support. It neither qualifies teachers nor emits production checkpoints; a fresh optimizer is part of its declared trial semantics.
- [gte_decoder_warm_start.create_warm_start](/home/barberb/lift_coding/external/ipfs_datasets/ipfs_datasets_py/logic/formalization/autoencoder/gte_decoder_warm_start.py:350) copies the complete learned384D decoder into a private768-input student and introduces only a768-to384 boundary. Its intermediate384D state is an adapted latent, not a GTE-small vector. `create_fresh_optimizer` starts empty Adam state and transfers no8D/384D moments.
- [gte_decoder_transfer_replay.export_decoder_transfer_batch](/home/barberb/lift_coding/external/ipfs_datasets/ipfs_datasets_py/logic/formalization/autoencoder/gte_decoder_transfer_replay.py:340) preserves original384D/8D donor behavior and emits reference-prefix logits as unqualified preparation. It bypasses new interfaces and does not create768D inputs or complete KD.
- [source_checkpoint_continuation_numeric_v1.run](/home/barberb/lift_coding/external/ipfs_datasets/ipfs_datasets_py/logic/formalization/autoencoder/source_checkpoint_continuation_numeric_v1.py:21) continues a compatible authenticated saved decoder. Adam starts empty because the saved source-v2 checkpoint lacks optimizer state. Selection uses supplied original validation rows, keeps the parent as initial best, and accepts no test rows.

The existing [decoder-length/distillation guide](/home/barberb/lift_coding/external/ipfs_datasets/docs/autoencoders/decoder_length_distillation.md:17) explicitly distinguishes a single-rule384D donor, fixed-schema sidecars, and factorized768D interfaces. Increasing output cap on the same40-token targets is not long-target learning. It reports a particular768D preparation with zero ready rows and zero optimizer updates; that observation does not prove no other768D experiment exists.

### Existing gradient diagnosis is a useful starting failure, not a new success

The guide's [exact gradient-spike replay section](/home/barberb/lift_coding/external/ipfs_datasets/docs/autoencoders/decoder_length_distillation.md:842) records four historical fits with340 updates each, eight deliberately tail-selected captured events, and exact combined optimizer-step replay followed by separate private token/count gradient reconciliation. The largest recorded preclip norm is7599.256; the token branch dominates, while the projection MSE is frozen and supplies no trainable gradient.

The same documented experiment reports0/48 exact validation paragraphs in every arm, selected epoch0, and no promotion. It explicitly does not prove a recurrent-Jacobian mechanism, monotonic sequence-length instability, fresh heldout improvement, or actual768D training. These are reported historical results, not independently replayed in this research.

This negative result changes the proposed next experiment: diagnose the known transition/spike and shared-condition interactions using the existing captured-event owners before claiming a new universal credit method. A large gradient is a localization observation, not proof that editing the corresponding tensors will improve source-faithful decoding.

### Later historical results supersede the early numerical frontier

The early0/48 result is not the latest result in the same guide. The later [generated-field/cadence study](/home/barberb/lift_coding/external/ipfs_datasets/docs/autoencoders/decoder_length_distillation.md:3361) includes actual numerical fits on8D/384D/768D inputs and substantially better final candidate outputs. Its saved [results.json](/home/barberb/lift_coding/external/ipfs_datasets/docs/implementation/reports/evidence/decoder-generated-field-training-r2-20261003/results.json) was directly read in this research:3425258 bytes, SHA-256 `149996bb6ce3b73b96cfc2b5f52eb310bc0d754713875b7e132d2d52d512cb3b`. The associated [manifest.json](/home/barberb/lift_coding/external/ipfs_datasets/docs/implementation/reports/evidence/decoder-generated-field-training-r2-20261003/manifest.json) is746329 bytes, SHA-256 `6c9819f5968d430070dc7e3dc1bdb9a5954da6d900857d7fa1c00db6b65bd8b7`.

For width768/seed2718, the saved last-attempt validation summaries report:

